# Upstash Redis, for the footer's visitor counter.
#
# Copy this file to .env.local and paste the values from Upstash. Whichever
# naming your database uses is fine — the route checks all three pairs, in
# this order. .env.local is gitignored.
#
# Direct signup at upstash.com:
UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL=
UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN=
#
# Older Vercel KV integration:
#   KV_REST_API_URL=
#   KV_REST_API_TOKEN=
#
# Vercel Marketplace (Storage tab) — note the lowercase `storage_` prefix:
#   storage_KV_REST_API_URL=
#   storage_KV_REST_API_TOKEN=
#
# Use the read-write token, not KV_REST_API_READ_ONLY_TOKEN — the counter
# needs INCR. The redis:// URLs (KV_URL, REDIS_URL) are for TCP clients and
# are not used here.
#
# Leave these unset and the counter simply doesn't render.
